IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `coa-core`
IMPORT `coa24-penalty`

-- coa24-tests-penalty.l4: tests for s 1125 and s 1131 (coa24-penalty.l4). Expected values are worked out by hand from the
-- text of the two sections. The pounds are TEST FIGURES (level 1 = 100 ... level 5 = 500, statutory maximum = 1000):
-- the Act does not state them and these stand for nothing.

§ `Test figures`

`the test amounts` MEANS `s 1125 amounts the Act leaves to other instruments` WITH
    `s 1125 level 1 on the standard scale, in pounds` IS 100
    `s 1125 level 2 on the standard scale, in pounds` IS 200
    `s 1125 level 3 on the standard scale, in pounds` IS 300
    `s 1125 level 4 on the standard scale, in pounds` IS 400
    `s 1125 level 5 on the standard scale, in pounds` IS 500
    `s 1125 the statutory maximum, in pounds` IS 1000

-- "a fine not exceeding level 5 on the standard scale and, for continued contravention, a daily default fine not exceeding
-- one-tenth of level 5 on the standard scale" (the shape of ss 1098E(5)(b) and 1098G(5)(b)).
`a penalty with a level 5 fine and a daily default fine of one-tenth of level 5` MEANS Penalty WITH
    `how convicted` IS `on summary conviction`
    `imprisonment not exceeding` IS NOTHING
    `fine not exceeding` IS JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` OF 5, 1)
    `daily default fine for continued contravention` IS JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` OF 5, 0.1)
    `imprisonment and fine together` IS FALSE

-- A fine of a stated level and no daily default fine.
`a penalty with a level 3 fine only` MEANS Penalty WITH
    `how convicted` IS `on summary conviction`
    `imprisonment not exceeding` IS NOTHING
    `fine not exceeding` IS JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` OF 3, 1)
    `daily default fine for continued contravention` IS NOTHING
    `imprisonment and fine together` IS FALSE

-- "a fine" without a stated limit (the England and Wales limb of ss 1098E(5)(a) and 1112(3)(a)) with a daily default fine.
`a penalty with an unlimited fine and a daily default fine of one-tenth of level 5` MEANS Penalty WITH
    `how convicted` IS `on summary conviction in England and Wales`
    `imprisonment not exceeding` IS NOTHING
    `fine not exceeding` IS JUST `a fine without a stated limit`
    `daily default fine for continued contravention` IS JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` OF 5, 0.1)
    `imprisonment and fine together` IS FALSE

§ `Tests for s 1125(1): the amount a fine limit stands for`

#ASSERT `s 1125(1) the section defines the daily default fine for the offence provision` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1125(1) the section defines the daily default fine for the offence provision` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

#ASSERT `s 1125(1) the fine limit in pounds` (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` OF 5, 1) `the test amounts` EQUALS JUST 500
#ASSERT `s 1125(1) the fine limit in pounds` (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` OF 5, 0.1) `the test amounts` EQUALS JUST 50
#ASSERT `s 1125(1) the fine limit in pounds` (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` OF 1, 1) `the test amounts` EQUALS JUST 100
#ASSERT `s 1125(1) the fine limit in pounds` (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` OF 2, 1) `the test amounts` EQUALS JUST 200
#ASSERT `s 1125(1) the fine limit in pounds` (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` OF 3, 1) `the test amounts` EQUALS JUST 300
#ASSERT `s 1125(1) the fine limit in pounds` (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` OF 4, 1) `the test amounts` EQUALS JUST 400
-- There is no level 6 on the standard scale as the amounts record has it: not covered.
#ASSERT `s 1125(1) the fine limit in pounds` (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` OF 6, 1) `the test amounts` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 1125(1) the fine limit in pounds` (`a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` OF 1) `the test amounts` EQUALS JUST 1000
#ASSERT `s 1125(1) the fine limit in pounds` (`a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` OF 0.2) `the test amounts` EQUALS JUST 200
#ASSERT `s 1125(1) the fine limit in pounds` (`a fine not exceeding an amount in pounds` OF 5000) `the test amounts` EQUALS JUST 5000
#ASSERT `s 1125(1) the fine limit in pounds` `a fine without a stated limit` `the test amounts` EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Tests for s 1125(2): the daily default fine`

-- First conviction: the former amount (level 5), not a daily one.
#ASSERT `s 1125(2) the fine limit that applies on this conviction` `a penalty with a level 5 fine and a daily default fine of one-tenth of level 5` FALSE EQUALS JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` OF 5, 1)
#ASSERT `s 1125(2) the limit applies for each day` `a penalty with a level 5 fine and a daily default fine of one-tenth of level 5` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Second or subsequent conviction: one-tenth of level 5 for each day, instead of the former amount.
#ASSERT `s 1125(2) the fine limit that applies on this conviction` `a penalty with a level 5 fine and a daily default fine of one-tenth of level 5` TRUE EQUALS JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` OF 5, 0.1)
#ASSERT `s 1125(2) the limit applies for each day` `a penalty with a level 5 fine and a daily default fine of one-tenth of level 5` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- No daily default fine in the offence provision: section 1125 does not speak.
#ASSERT `s 1125(2) the fine limit that applies on this conviction` `a penalty with a level 3 fine only` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 1125(2) the limit applies for each day` `a penalty with a level 3 fine only` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- The most that can be imposed. First conviction, 3 days of continued contravention: still just level 5 (500).
#ASSERT `s 1125(2) the most the person can be fined on this conviction, in pounds` `a penalty with a level 5 fine and a daily default fine of one-tenth of level 5` FALSE 3 `the test amounts` EQUALS JUST 500
-- Second conviction, 3 days: one-tenth of 500 is 50 a day, so 150.
#ASSERT `s 1125(2) the most the person can be fined on this conviction, in pounds` `a penalty with a level 5 fine and a daily default fine of one-tenth of level 5` TRUE 3 `the test amounts` EQUALS JUST 150
-- Second conviction, 1 day: 50.
#ASSERT `s 1125(2) the most the person can be fined on this conviction, in pounds` `a penalty with a level 5 fine and a daily default fine of one-tenth of level 5` TRUE 1 `the test amounts` EQUALS JUST 50
-- Second conviction, 0 days continued: nothing accrues.
#ASSERT `s 1125(2) the most the person can be fined on this conviction, in pounds` `a penalty with a level 5 fine and a daily default fine of one-tenth of level 5` TRUE 0 `the test amounts` EQUALS JUST 0
-- No daily default fine: not covered by section 1125.
#ASSERT `s 1125(2) the most the person can be fined on this conviction, in pounds` `a penalty with a level 3 fine only` TRUE 3 `the test amounts` EQUALS NOTHING
-- An unlimited former amount has no number: first conviction gives NOTHING, second gives the daily total.
#ASSERT `s 1125(2) the most the person can be fined on this conviction, in pounds` `a penalty with an unlimited fine and a daily default fine of one-tenth of level 5` FALSE 3 `the test amounts` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 1125(2) the most the person can be fined on this conviction, in pounds` `a penalty with an unlimited fine and a daily default fine of one-tenth of level 5` TRUE 3 `the test amounts` EQUALS JUST 150

§ `Tests for s 1131`

#ASSERT `s 1131(1) the section applies to the provision` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1131(1) the section applies to the provision` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- An offence committed before 2 May 2022: six months, whatever the general limit is.
#ASSERT `s 1131(2) the term of imprisonment the provision refers to` (Date 1 5 2022) (JUST (Period OF 12, Months)) EQUALS JUST (Period OF 6, Months)
#ASSERT `s 1131(2) the term of imprisonment the provision refers to` (Date 31 12 2021) NOTHING EQUALS JUST (Period OF 6, Months)
-- Committed on 2 May 2022 or later: no substitution; the general limit (a test figure of 12 months here) governs.
#ASSERT `s 1131(2) the term of imprisonment the provision refers to` (Date 2 5 2022) (JUST (Period OF 12, Months)) EQUALS JUST (Period OF 12, Months)
#ASSERT `s 1131(2) the term of imprisonment the provision refers to` (Date 3 5 2022) (JUST (Period OF 12, Months)) EQUALS JUST (Period OF 12, Months)
-- On or after 2 May 2022 with no general limit supplied: the Act does not state it, so not covered.
#ASSERT `s 1131(2) the term of imprisonment the provision refers to` (Date 2 5 2022) NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
